From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: a733: BL31 in SRAM at 0x62000, no SCP

489a44f885 moves BL31 to DRAM at 0x48000000 and adds an SCP image at
0x48100000, for a prebuilt BL31 of 115 677 B that does not fit the SRAM
slot. A BL31 built from TF-A source does: it links at 0x62000, with
BL31_LIMIT 0x70000. Nothing on this chain starts the E902, so the FIT
carries no SCP image. Both defaults go back to what they were before that
commit.

The SPL runs from SRAM at 0x47060 and carries the DRAM blob, which the
boot hook copies to SUNXI_LIBDRAM_BASE (0x90000) before anything else
runs. With SPL_MAX_SIZE 0x49000 and a blob of 232 409 B, the blob's copy
inside the SPL image covers 0x57487-0x7fc39 wherever the linker puts it,
so loading BL31 into 0x62000-0x70000 overwrites no part of the SPL that
is still in use.

Assisted-by: Claude
Link: https://github.com/radxa/u-boot/commit/489a44f885e3eecb8e96dac8eb8f6f6f0231c4ed
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
index d090c1fac29..c6c0edaa6bb 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -265,7 +265,7 @@ config SUNXI_BL31_BASE
 	default 0x40000000 if MACH_SUN50I_H616
 	default 0x00104000 if SUN50I_GEN_H6
 	default 0x00054000 if MACH_SUN55I_A523
-	default 0x48000000 if MACH_SUN60I_A733
+	default 0x00062000 if MACH_SUN60I_A733
 	default 0x0
 	help
 	  Address where BL31 (TF-A) is loaded, or zero if BL31 is not used.
@@ -274,7 +274,6 @@ config SUNXI_SCP_BASE
 	hex
 	default 0x00050000 if MACH_SUN50I || MACH_SUN50I_H5
 	default 0x00114000 if MACH_SUN50I_H6
-	default 0x48100000 if MACH_SUN60I_A733
 	default 0x0
 	help
 	  Address where SCP firmware is loaded, or zero if it is not used.
